WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.632 --> 00:00:04.854
- [Man] What you're seeing
was built by one man

00:00:04.854 --> 00:00:07.521
pebble by pebble, over 33 years.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.501
One morning, mailman Ferdinand
Cheval stumbled across

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:19.141
an interesting looking
stone on his delivery route.

00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:23.308
He picked it up, and from
there, an obsession began.

00:00:24.195 --> 00:00:26.296
Using stones he collected on his walk,

00:00:26.296 --> 00:00:28.958
Cheval worked each night
without any formal training

00:00:28.958 --> 00:00:32.708
to build what is now
called the Palais Idéal.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.026
The final structure is 85
feet long and 300 feet high.

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:43.006
It mingles Chinese, Algerian,
and Northern European

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:46.688
influences to create a fantastic
and completely original

00:00:46.688 --> 00:00:48.271
castle of grottos.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:56.284
He opened the palace in 1870
for the public to enjoy.

00:00:57.171 --> 00:00:59.064
In his own words he says,

00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:01.394
"You start wondering if you
have not been carried away

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.661
into a fantastic dream, with boundaries

00:01:03.661 --> 00:01:06.494
beyond the scope of imagination."

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:11.502
And this incredible,
bizarre, and unique place

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:15.669
does look like something you
could only see in a dream.

